# --- Power Pages deploy output ---
# Regenerated by `pac pages upload-code-site`: content-hashed bundles and the pac
# manifests churn on every deploy, so tracking them on more than one branch produces
# unavoidable merge conflicts (which is exactly what bit us). They stay on disk for
# whoever deploys and are recreated on the next upload. Meaningful site config
# (site-settings/, table-permissions/, web-roles/, content-snippets/, page-templates/, …)
# stays tracked.
.powerpages-site/.portalconfig/manifest.yml
.powerpages-site/.portalconfig/*-manifest.yml
.powerpages-site/web-files/index-*/
.powerpages-site/web-files/SignagePage-*/
.powerpages-site/web-files/ea7-logo-*/
.powerpages-site/web-files/index.html/
.powerpages-site/web-files/*.js/
.powerpages-site/web-pages/home/content-pages/en-US/Home.webpage.copy.html

# Solution export artifacts
*.zip
# BC sample responses (real customer data)
docs/bc-samples/
